1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,399
I then spend my first couple hours at my desk.
接着，最开始的几个小时我会坐在办公桌前。

2
00:00:02,399 --> 00:00:08,880
Checking in on the team in slack putting out any flyers and helping where I can and adding in my two cents.
在Slack上跟进团队、处理问题，能帮就帮，再提提自己的意见。

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:14,399
Then I'll usually go through my inbox I seriously spend way too much time in my inbox.
然后我通常会处理收件箱，我花在收件箱上的时间实在太多了。

4
00:00:14,399 --> 00:00:20,339
And it's usually to manage things like suppliers travel plans and a big one is brand sponsors.
通常是处理供应商、旅行计划，还有很大一块是品牌赞助商。

5
00:00:20,339 --> 00:00:25,430
We're lucky enough to have more brand partners in our inbox than we can actually take on right now.
幸运的是，来找我们的品牌伙伴比我们目前能承接的还多。

6
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,080
It's part of the reason why we need to expand the team.
这也是我们需要扩大团队的部分原因。

7
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:31,980
So it takes a lot of my time fielding these emails even with my team's help.
因此即使有团队帮忙，应对这些邮件还是占用我很多时间。

8
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:37,080
And I actually say no to at least 90 of sponsorship requests if not more.
我实际上会拒绝至少90%的赞助请求，甚至更多。

9
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:44,700
Then I'll move on to running the routine shopify store and add checks and help out with our students inside our mastery programs.
接着，我会检查Shopify店铺及其他项目，并帮助我们课程项目里的学生。

10
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,220
Which is our marketing and online business course.
那是我们的营销和线上生意课程。

11
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:49,320
At this point it's about 11 am.
这时大约是上午11点。

12
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:53,399
And before I take a break I'll usually get started on the fun creative work.
休息之前，我通常会先开始做那些有趣的创作工作。

13
00:00:53,399 --> 00:00:57,540
So the photography the filming and the tech reviews which I absolutely love creating.
也就是摄影、拍片和科技产品评测，我特别喜欢创作这些。

14
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:01,200
I usually buy most of the tech I review you out of my pocket.
我评测的大多数科技产品都是自己掏钱买的。

15
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:05,339
But we also get sent a load of cool gadgets from all sorts of brands too.
不过，各类品牌也会寄来许多有趣的小设备。

16
00:01:05,339 --> 00:01:08,399
And no single day is the same when it comes to filming.
说到拍摄，每一天都不一样。

17
00:01:08,399 --> 00:01:15,059
Sometimes I'm in this dedicated studio space sometimes I'm out and in balance sometimes I'm even overseas filming.
有时我在专门的工作室，有时在外面，有时甚至去海外拍摄。

18
00:01:15,059 --> 00:01:17,100
And it's a lot more work than most people think.
这比大多数人想的费力得多。

19
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:25,080
Setting up all the camera gear setting up the new tech and getting literally hours of cinematic footage can be pretty physically tiring.
架设相机设备、布置新产品、拍上数小时电影感画面，身体会很累。

20
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:30,229
But it's really rewarding and as long as you guys enjoy the end product that is all that matters.
不过很有成就感，只要大家喜欢最终作品，就值得了。

21
00:01:30,239 --> 00:01:32,940
My work day is always so dynamic and different.
我的工作日总是变化很多，很不一样。

22
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:39,660
And as someone who finds it really hard to stay put in an office cubicle it suits my working style really well.
我很难一直坐在办公室隔间里，所以这种工作方式很适合我。

23
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:44,280
Today isn't as busy on the filming front so I'm going to head over to a local cafe.
今天拍摄任务没那么忙，我打算去附近咖啡馆。

24
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:50,810
Before I drive over this is the robot vacuum cleaner I turned on so I can come back to a clean office.
开车过去前，我开了扫地机器人，这样回来办公室就是干净的。

25
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:54,420
Gadgets like these are such a lifesaver and save me a lot of time.
这样的设备真是救星，帮我省下很多时间。

26
00:01:54,420 --> 00:02:01,320
It's really nice also to have the privilege of constantly changing up the space so work never gets dull.
能不断换一换工作场所也是种难得的便利，让工作不至于无聊。

27
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:04,799
I usually go with my partner or a friend to catch up over lunch.
我通常和伴侣或朋友一起午餐，顺便聊聊近况。

28
00:02:04,799 --> 00:02:13,920
And then continue with other work over there like video scripting managing incoming contracts and a routine check on the team over slack and similar things like that.
然后在那里继续写视频脚本、处理新合同、在Slack上例行跟进团队等工作。

29
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:20,699
Research shows most people can't sustain more than four hours of deep work per day myself included.
作者说，研究显示大多数人每天无法维持超过四小时深度工作，包括他自己。

30
00:02:20,699 --> 00:02:25,920
So I work in blocks and I try to break it up otherwise it's just too much of a struggle.
所以我分时段工作，并尽量穿插休息，不然会很吃力。

31
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:31,070
But yeah this was a nice treat today this local cafe does really good specialty drinks and coffee.
不过今天真是享受，这家附近的咖啡馆特色饮品和咖啡做得很好。

32
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:34,740
We had a couple fresh sandwiches sodas and scones.
我们吃了新鲜三明治，喝了汽水，还吃了司康。

33
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:37,379
And we definitely don't get to work from a cafe daily.
而且我们肯定不是每天都能在咖啡馆办公。

34
00:02:37,379 --> 00:02:42,540
And there are actually often times I work right through lunch depending on what I'm doing.
实际上有时会看任务情况，一路工作到午餐时间也不停。

35
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:45,720
By the time we get back home it's about 5 p m today.
今天我们到家时，大约下午五点。

36
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:51,480
It's been really hard to just switch off and stop working right in the evenings especially when you run your own business.
晚上想停下工作、切换到休息状态很难，尤其是经营自己的生意时。

37
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:56,090
My partner is the same since she has a lot of incoming work and projects with her business too.
我伴侣也一样，她自己的生意也有许多新工作和项目。

38
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:59,819
So force function to wind down has been cooking healthy dinners together.
所以，一起做健康晚餐成了让我们放松下来的方式。

39
00:02:59,819 --> 00:03:05,520
And to save time we've got into the habit of cooking hello fresh dinners and it's been really enjoyable.
为了省时间，我们养成做HelloFresh晚餐的习惯，感觉很愉快。

40
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,910
This isn't sponsored by them at all by the way.
顺便说一下，这段完全不是他们赞助的。

41
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,560
We've just been really enjoying hello fresh for months now.
我们只是几个月来一直很喜欢用HelloFresh。

42
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:18,920
Tonight we're cooking sesame oven baked fries sichuan glazed pork meatballs and a japanese salad on the side and it was freaking delicious.
今晚做的是芝麻烤薯条、川味酱汁猪肉丸，旁边配日式沙拉，真是好吃极了。
